## Define the User Journey: If I am a user, what exactly do I do?
1. Open application
2. Upload Resume
3. Paste Job Description
4. Click "Analyze"
5. Backend receives data
6. Resume/JD processed
7. AI analyzes compatibility
8. Result stored in MySQL
9. Frontend displays result

## Convert Workflow Into Features(Don't build everything)
-- For Version 1:
Feature 1: Analyze Resume
Feature 2: Save Analysis History
Feature 3: View Previous Analyses
Don't add: Login
            Payments
            Admin dashboard
            Notifications
            Chatbot
            100 AI agents
            Mobile app

### Start With the Database [What information must our system remember?]
users | resumes | job_descriptions | analyses

-- For a first version, even:
## analyses
id
resume_text
job_description
match_score
strengths
missing_skills
suggestions
created_at

CREATE DATABASE resume_analyzer;
USE resume_analyzer;

CREATE TABLE analyses (
    analysis_id BIGINT PRIMARY KEY AUTO_INCREMENT,
    resume_text LONGTEXT NOT NULL,
    job_description LONGTEXT NOT NULL,
    match_score DECIMAL(5,2),
    strengths JSON,
    missing_skills JSON,
    suggestions JSON,
    created_at DATETIME DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
);

